Notice that all notes are defined in ratios, the standard "equal-tempered" scale has each semitone equal to a ratio of the twelfth root of 2, or 1.05946. So, for example, a fifth is 1.05946 to the 7th power (seven semitones in a musical fifth) or 1.49831. All values are aproximate numbers rounded to the 5th decimal digit.

CHROMATIC Ratios & Scale Intervals:

1 semitone = 2^(1/12) = ~1.05946

A fifth = 2^(7/12) = ~1.49831

C = 1 = Root
Db = 1.05946 = minor 2nd
D = 1.12246 = Major 2nd
Eb = 1.18921 = minor 3rd
E = 1.25992 = Major 3rd
F = 1.33483 = Perfect 4th
Gb = 1.41421 = dim 5th
G = 1.49831 = Perfect 5th
Ab = 1.58740 = minor 6th
A = 1.68179 = Major 6th
Bb = 1.78180 = minor 7th
B = 1.88775 = Major 7th
C = 2 = Octave
